From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,s8000-display-pipe: Add the A8's
 eDP transmitter

The iPad mini 4 is an A8 (T7000) board whose panel link is eDP, not MIPI
DSI: its Apple device tree has a displayport node ("displayport,t7000",
0x206700000) with an lpdp-phy and an eDP panel, where the iPod touch 6
and the iPhone 6 have mipi-dsim. Allow the DisplayPort transmitter's
window as an optional fourth "dp" region of "apple,t7000-display-pipe",
as the A9's pipe has it, so that a board can say which link it drives.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml     | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
index b4b4394..ae95259 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
@@ -134,19 +134,25 @@ allOf:
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
-          maxItems: 3
+          minItems: 3
+          maxItems: 4
           items:
             - description:
                 ADP window, with the control and interrupt registers, the
                 parameter FIFO port and the pipe layer registers
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), first window
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), second window
+            - description:
+                DisplayPort transmitter (displayport), on the boards whose
+                panel link is eDP
         reg-names:
-          maxItems: 3
+          minItems: 3
+          maxItems: 4
           items:
             - const: adp
             - const: dart0
             - const: dart1
+            - const: dp
         interrupts:
           maxItems: 5
           items:
